-- title:
--   Volume of a closed product cube in $\mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d$
-- statement:
--   Work on the product space $\mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d$ with its product Lebesgue measure. For
--   a real number $h$ and a pair $u = (u_1,u_2) \in \mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d$, let
--   $A_h^{(2)}(u) := \texttt{closedCube\_two } h\ u$ be the closed product cube of side $h$ at $u$, that
--   is the product $A_h(u_1)\times A_h(u_2)$ of the two closed cubes of side $h$. Let $h \ge 0$. Then
--
--   $$\lambda_{2d}\big(A^{(2)}_h(u)\big) \;=\; h^{\,2d},$$
--
--   as an element of $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   The product cubes are the tiles used to differentiate a function of a *pair*, such as
--   $(s,t)\mapsto (f(s)-f(t))^2 k(s,t)$; their volume is the normalisation of the corresponding tile
--   average, and it is the factor by which a sum over pairs of lattice points converts into an integral
--   over $\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The ambient type is the product `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) × EuclideanSpace ℝ
--   (Fin d)`, not `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (2d))`: its norm is the maximum of the two factors rather than
--   the Euclidean norm of the concatenation, which is why the product cubes are rebuilt directly instead
--   of transported along an equivalence. As for the single cube, $h = 0$ is allowed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/LebesgueDiff2.lean#L44-L48

